# Luigi held-item architecture

- Implement transfer, positioning, swap, hide/restore, and despawn behavior generically through `!LuigiHeldItemIndex` (`$41B82E`).
- Do not add Luigi-specific fixes to individual carryables such as `Key.asm` or `KoopaShell.asm` for positioning/despawn.
- Mario↔held-item rules are keyed by `!LuigiHeldItemIndex` (TXA compare, not `$15E9|!addr`): no grab; ignore entirely when Mario carries Luigi (`14C8=$0B`); bounceable shells may stomp-bounce Mario without leaving Luigi's hands; **spin / Yoshi** on a held shell spinkills it and clears `!LuigiHeldItemIndex`.
- While Luigi owns an item, set `$167A` bit 7 to suppress vanilla Mario interaction; restore it for vanilla items returned to Mario. Otherwise vanilla shells can award points/grab before Luigi's handler runs.
- Never transfer a held index whose `!14C8` is below `$08`; spinkill must clear both ownership indices if either aliases the killed slot.
- Reject `$1498=$08` same-frame pickups when a swap starts; return that sprite to `$09` instead of replacing Luigi's existing held item.
- Luigi↔Mario-held-item rules are keyed by `!MarioHeldItemIndex`: non-shell carryables keep normal platform/solid behavior (Luigi can stand on a carried Key); held shells use bounce-only handling that never kicks, spawns a Koopa, or changes ownership.
- Shell detection is generic via `SetCarryIfShell` (vanilla `$04`–`$0C` / `$DA`–`$DF`, plus all custom shell IDs in `list.txt`). Do not special-case one color in Key/shell asm for Mario↔held behavior.
- `tools/pixi/sprites/!!Luigi/Luigi.asm` owns gameplay transfer, teleport lifecycle, Mario↔held-item interact, and post-physics item positioning on SA-1.
- `tools/uberasmtool/library/SyncLuigiHeldItem.asm` owns SNES-side pre-draw projection.
- `MoveLuigiToFront.asm` owns only slot reordering and held-slot index remapping. Level glue calls the sync library immediately afterward because UberASM Tool does not link library-to-library dependencies.
- Preserve the established facing offsets (`+$000B` / `-$000B`), fixed-point projection, fractions, spin facing, and Mario-carry behavior unless intentionally redesigning them.
- SNES-side UberASM must use SA-1 DP mirrors (`$30B6`, `$309E`, `$3094`, `$30D1`, `$307D`, `$3076`, `$309D`).
- SA-1 PIXI code that accesses `$30xx` mirrors while DBR is not guaranteed must force long addressing (`LDA.l` / `SBC.l`), not DBR-relative absolute addressing.
- Preserve processor width at library boundaries. Never index the two-entry facing-offset table with width-sensitive `LDX $00`; branch to immediate 16-bit offsets instead.
- Before converting a held byte index with `TAY`/`TAX`, force 8-bit index width under `PHP : SEP #$30` and restore it on every return.
